# Selected Record Templates

These are reusable templates, not completed project records. Create a concrete record only when requested, required by an existing workflow, or useful for preserving a material investigation, decision, transition, or acceptance result. Prefer an existing project format; link its source instead of creating a duplicate hierarchy.

{{recordTemplateLinks}}

Copy only the relevant template to a task-appropriate location, give it a meaningful name, and replace prompts with observed facts or explicitly unknown/not applicable items. Make local links relative to the new record's location. Do not prefill approval, installed versions, commands, ownership, or successful results without evidence. Reuse already granted authorization within scope; documenting it does not require granting it again.

Keep sensitive evidence in permitted locations and use safe references or redacted summaries. A record does not authorize delegation, migration execution, publication, production access, or permission changes. These templates prescribe no language, directory layout, runtime, service, architecture style, or test framework.
